<title>UK: LIFFE white sugar drifts, ends mixed.</title>
<headline>LIFFE white sugar drifts, ends mixed.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-06-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>White sugar futures drifted back in lacklustre late Wednesday trading, ending the session mixed, although spot August was still steadier.</p>
<p>Traders said there was little to excite the sugar trade, both in London and New York, and price movements were fairly light.</p>
<p>At the close August was off 30 cents at $322.90, but other positions were $0.10 to $0.70 higher. Turnover was a thin 1,448 lots.</p>
<p>--London Newsroom +44 171 542 8064</p>
